WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.373
The secret garden was not the only one that Dickon worked in.

2
00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:11.301
At his family's cottage on the moor was a garden surrounded by a low wall.

3
00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:15.030
Dickon grew all sorts of vegetables and flowers there.

4
00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:20.833
When he worked in the garden after supper, his mother liked to sit on the wall and talk to him.

5
00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:25.581
The children had agreed that Dickon's mother could know about the secret garden.

6
00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:33.960
So Dickon told her everything: from how Mary had found the key to what Ben had said when he discovered them in the garden.

7
00:00:33.961 --> 00:00:38.859
"It's a good thing that girl came to the manor," said Mother.

8
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.950
"That's made her well and saved Colin. Standing on his feet!

9
00:00:44.951 --> 00:00:49.116
What does everyone at the manor think about his feeling so well?"

10
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:52.074
"They don't know what to think."

11
00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:54.129
And that was true.

12
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:58.203
The nurse was the first to notice that Colin was eating more.

13
00:00:58.204 --> 00:01:02.098
"You didn't used to eat," she said to him.

14
00:01:02.099 --> 00:01:05.671
"So many things bothered your stomach."

15
00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:09.946
"Nothing bothers my stomach these days," said Colin.

16
00:01:09.947 --> 00:01:16.333
The nurse gave him a strange look, and Colin realized he shouldn't appear too well just yet.

17
00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:20.589
"I mean, just a few things bother my stomach now."

18
00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:25.222
When Dr. Craven arrived, he asked a lot of questions.

19
00:01:25.223 --> 00:01:30.027
"You stay out in the gardens a great deal. Where do you go?"

20
00:01:30.028 --> 00:01:32.820
"I go to a place I like."

21
00:01:32.821 --> 00:01:36.918
"You seem to be gaining weight, and your color is better."

22
00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:41.361
"Perhaps I am feverish." Colin put on an air of gloom.

23
00:01:41.362 --> 00:01:45.810
"People who are not going to live are often . . . different."

24
00:01:45.811 --> 00:01:50.619
Dr. Craven shook his head. "You're not feverish.

25
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:56.120
If you keep getting better, we will have to tell your father of this remarkable improvement."

26
00:01:56.121 --> 00:02:00.091
But Colin wasn't ready to share the news with his father.

27
00:02:00.092 --> 00:02:03.884
"I won't have him told!" he said fiercely.

28
00:02:03.885 --> 00:02:07.227
"It will only disappoint him if I get worse again.

29
00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:10.936
You're making me angry, and I'm feeling worse already."

30
00:02:10.937 --> 00:02:16.437
"Hush, my boy. No letters will be written without your permission."

31
00:02:16.438 --> 00:02:21.970
Dr. Craven studied Colin with a puzzled look, and then he went on his way.

32
00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:26.068
Mary and Colin were quite alarmed after the doctor's visit.

33
00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:31.072
"I want to surprise my father by walking into his study," Colin told her.

34
00:02:31.073 --> 00:02:36.614
"We must pretend that you are much worse than you really are," said Mary.

35
00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:43.504
So starting that day, Colin made sure to complain when the footman carried him downstairs to his wheelchair.

36
00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:49.191
Mary made sympathetic noises and hovered over him as if he were terribly ill.

37
00:02:49.192 --> 00:02:51.775
There was only one problem.

38
00:02:51.776 --> 00:02:56.522
Mary and Colin were growing, and they were very hungry.

39
00:02:56.523 --> 00:03:02.672
They didn't dare ask for more food because the servants would realize Colin was getting better.

40
00:03:02.673 --> 00:03:07.958
One evening Dickon told his mother about this problem, and she had an idea.

41
00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.836
"When you go to see them in the morning, take a pail of new milk.

42
00:03:12.837 --> 00:03:17.565
I'll bake a crusty loaf of bread or some buns."

43
00:03:17.566 --> 00:03:22.265
The next day Dickon surprised Mary and Colin with the milk and buns.

44
00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:27.122
"There's magic in your mother, just as there is in you," said Colin.

45
00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:30.490
"It makes her think of ways to do nice things.

46
00:03:30.491 --> 00:03:33.569
Tell her we are grateful, Dickon."

47
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.964
Dickon brought them food every day.

48
00:03:36.965 --> 00:03:43.082
After a while Mary and Colin remembered that Mrs. Sowerby had a large family to feed.

49
00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:46.101
So they began to pay her for their food.

50
00:03:46.102 --> 00:03:50.390
Then Dickon made a discovery in the woods outside the garden.

51
00:03:50.391 --> 00:03:57.148
There was a deep hole where he could build a tiny oven out of stones for roasting potatoes and eggs.

52
00:03:57.149 --> 00:04:00.165
Now they could really have a feast!

53
00:04:00.166 --> 00:04:04.468
Of course, when they went inside for lunch, they weren't hungry.

54
00:04:04.469 --> 00:04:09.503
"Look!" said Mrs. Medlock to the nurse as she carried away their dishes.

55
00:04:09.504 --> 00:04:12.399
"They've hardly touched their food.

56
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.384
The cook is afraid Mr. Craven will blame her if they starve themselves to death."

57
00:04:18.385 --> 00:04:23.013
The nurse saved the tray of uneaten food to show Dr. Craven.

58
00:04:23.014 --> 00:04:26.697
He was very puzzled when he came to examine Colin.

59
00:04:26.698 --> 00:04:29.523
"I'm sorry to hear that you are not eating.

60
00:04:29.524 --> 00:04:34.528
This will not do. You will lose all the weight that you've gained."

61
00:04:34.529 --> 00:04:37.436
"I told you I wasn't well."

62
00:04:37.437 --> 00:04:44.929
Mary started to laugh, but quickly turned her giggle into a cough.

63
00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.671
Dr. Craven left the children together and went to talk to Mrs. Medlock.

64
00:04:49.672 --> 00:04:54.227
"Going without food seems to agree with them, so I guess we shouldn't worry.

65
00:04:54.228 --> 00:04:57.497
That boy is a new creature."

66
00:04:57.498 --> 00:05:03.281
"And so is that girl. Mary is even beginning to look pretty.

67
00:05:03.282 --> 00:05:08.899
She used to be so unhappy, but now she and Colin laugh together all the time.

68
00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.261
Maybe they're growing fat on laughter."

69
00:05:12.262 --> 00:05:19.647
"Then let them laugh," said Dr. Craven.

